From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 16:33:52 +0000
Subject: MIPS: intel-mips: enable pinctrl, GPIO LEDs and buttons in
 grx500_defconfig

Turn on the pieces the freshly described xRX500 pin controller and GPIO
banks need, so the in-tree defconfig produces a kernel that can actually
drive a board's front panel:

 - CONFIG_PINCTRL / CONFIG_PINCTRL_EQUILIBRIUM. PINCTRL is a plain
   menuconfig with no default, so it has to be stated explicitly;
   PINCTRL_EQUILIBRIUM then selects PINMUX, PINCONF, GENERIC_PINCONF,
   GENERIC_PINCTRL_GROUPS, GENERIC_PINMUX_FUNCTIONS, GPIOLIB,
   GPIO_GENERIC and GPIOLIB_IRQCHIP on its own.

 - CONFIG_NEW_LEDS / LEDS_CLASS / LEDS_GPIO for the gpio-leds nodes,
   plus LEDS_TRIGGERS with the timer, default-on and netdev triggers --
   the three the status-LED conventions on these boards rely on
   (heartbeat-style activity, "on while running", and a link/activity
   LED bound to a netdev).

 - CONFIG_INPUT / INPUT_KEYBOARD / KEYBOARD_GPIO_POLLED for the
   gpio-keys-polled nodes, and INPUT_EVDEV so a button press is
   actually observable from userspace on a bare defconfig kernel --
   without an event handler the input device exists but reports
   nowhere. INPUT_KEYBOARD was previously explicitly disabled.

Note for downstream users: distributions that replace the in-kernel
button handling with their own (OpenWrt's gpio-button-hotplug binds the
same "gpio-keys-polled" compatible) must leave KEYBOARD_GPIO_POLLED off
in their own config or the two will fight over the device.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/configs/grx500_defconfig b/arch/mips/configs/grx500_defconfig
index c81e5195923f..c393e0431518 100644
--- a/arch/mips/configs/grx500_defconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/configs/grx500_defconfig
@@ -76,7 +76,10 @@ CONFIG_ATM_BR2684=m
 CONFIG_BLK_DEV_RAM=y
 CONFIG_BLK_DEV_RAM_COUNT=4
 CONFIG_BLK_DEV_RAM_SIZE=8192
-# CONFIG_INPUT_KEYBOARD is not set
+CONFIG_INPUT=y
+CONFIG_INPUT_EVDEV=y
+CONFIG_INPUT_KEYBOARD=y
+CONFIG_KEYBOARD_GPIO_POLLED=y
 # CONFIG_INPUT_MOUSE is not set
 # CONFIG_SERIO is not set
 # CONFIG_CONSOLE_TRANSLATIONS is not set
@@ -85,10 +88,19 @@ CONFIG_BLK_DEV_RAM_SIZE=8192
 # CONFIG_DEVMEM is not set
 CONFIG_SERIAL_LANTIQ=y
 # CONFIG_HW_RANDOM is not set
+CONFIG_PINCTRL=y
+CONFIG_PINCTRL_EQUILIBRIUM=y
 # CONFIG_HWMON is not set
 # CONFIG_VGA_CONSOLE is not set
 # CONFIG_HID is not set
 # CONFIG_USB_SUPPORT is not set
+CONFIG_NEW_LEDS=y
+CONFIG_LEDS_CLASS=y
+CONFIG_LEDS_GPIO=y
+CONFIG_LEDS_TRIGGERS=y
+CONFIG_LEDS_TRIGGER_TIMER=y
+CONFIG_LEDS_TRIGGER_DEFAULT_ON=y
+CONFIG_LEDS_TRIGGER_NETDEV=y
 # CONFIG_VIRTIO_MENU is not set
 # CONFIG_MIPS_PLATFORM_DEVICES is not set
 CONFIG_INTEL_CGU_CLK=y
